ment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "255a849a8c9f61b303791e91aeb01b41a1b547d5798920237a506eab85b098cf", "hash": "2b5e09930d9517f0f59dfc8f083899b8827b77c20aa0493da942debd9472a5b5"}, {"seq": 3224, "time": "2026-10-29T06:36:08.018722+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":19,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-acc474f466ab44f8\",\"previous_head\":\"023d791700b0cf187bdaec24fc69a781be24425122377d1e270d98e2de6a99a4\",\"process_id\":2451,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-acc474f466ab44f8", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "023d791700b0cf187bdaec24fc69a781be24425122377d1e270d98e2de6a99a4", "hash": "255a849a8c9f61b303791e91aeb01b41a1b547d5798920237a506eab85b098cf"}, {"seq